[Music]  hey everyone welcome to another  installment of harry potter theory  today i'm excited to be discussing the  major differences between the book and  film versions of drum roll please  harry potter  yes that's right today i'll be going  over the biggest variations between  harry as depicted in the novels versus  the movies right so as you may have seen  of the last few weeks i've released a  couple of other videos addressing the  book to film differences of other harry  potter characters specifically i've  shared my thoughts on the largest  discrepancies between the novel and  movie depictions of both hermione and  ron  and if you have yet to watch them i  encourage you to check them out and  share your thoughts with me in the  comments you can find both of these  videos right here on the harry potter  theory channel anyway for those of you  who have already watched the last couple  of videos on hermione and ron you may  have seen in the comments there were  quite a few requests for me to evaluate  the major differences between harry the  chosen one himself so without further  ado let's dig into it major difference  number one his overall attitude  when comparing the novel version of  harry potter to his counterpart in the  films one of the most noticeable  differences between the two is his  overall demeanor if you asked anyone  who's a fan of the books to describe  harry's character i'm willing to bet  that most of them would tell you that he  actually has a bit of an attitude  problem in the novels harry is  unapologetically sarcastic and he's  frequently getting himself in trouble by  being a bit of a smart mouth this is not  to say that the movie version of harry  doesn't get into his share of hot water  after all the main plot lines behind  each and every harry potter installment  is based on harry and the danger he  finds himself in but in the books the  trouble that harry gets into is  different somehow  novel harry seems to care very little  for the repercussions of some of his  actions a classical trait of  gryffindor's  whereas movie harry often seems like a  bit of a goody goody i'm sure every now  and again daniel radcliffe the actor who  portrayed harry potter in the movie  series delivers a bit of a cheeky line  or two and in these moments we see some  defiance speak out but where the movies  really lean into the angst and darkness  of harry's character the book showcased  him as a cheekier and more sharp-witted  young wizard  some fans have even gone so far as  sadeem novel harry as sassy and a bit of  a delinquent in the movies harry's  character also seems to be a little more  self-centered  he feels sorry for himself a lot more  and doesn't seem to really possess the  charisma of a natural-born leader like  he does in the books  major difference number two his magical  aptitude  in the movies harry is shown as being  magically gifted at most things almost  immediately  he's good or at least not bad at  basically everything he tries from  spells to flying  in the novels however harry's only  innate magical talent is his ability to  ride a broomstick he works hard for  everything else such as casting his  patronus and overcoming a boggart  as mentioned in my video about the  differences between novel and film ron  there's also the discrepancy between how  the two boys perform in school in the  books ron and harry both received  average marks but in the movies harry  seems to do much better in school than  ron  this creates somewhat of a problem in  the half-blood prince before in the  novels it's quite clear why harry needed  the notes written into the potions  textbook that he acquires by chance  in the film it doesn't make as much  sense why finding this text was so  beneficial to him  sure it makes him really awesome at this  class but it's more like he goes from an  a or b to an a plus  whereas in the novels the textbook saves  him from completely failing the class  major difference number three his  relationship with iran  another major difference which i also  brought up in my video discussing ron is  how the friendship between ron and harry  is portrayed  in the novels harry's best mate is  unquestionably wrong in fact in the  beginning of the book version of the  philosopher's stone harry doesn't even  like hermione he finds her annoying and  insufferable but in the movies he seems  to rely on his friendship with hermione  a lot more than he relies on ron this  may be because in the films ron is  depicted as kind of a buffoon and  hermione is the one with all the answers  so of course when dealing with serious  situations like defeating voldemort and  saving all of wizardkind it wouldn't  have made much sense from an audience  perspective for harry to seek advice  from ron whose only role in the films  seems to be comic relief we also miss  out on a lot of harry's relationship  with the weasley family as a whole  which of course impacts how his  friendship with ron is viewed  in the books harry spends a lot of time  with ron's family who embrace him  wholeheartedly while some of this can be  seen in the films it's usually harry and  hermione who are there not just harry  implying that it's not just harry and  ron who are super close but rather all  three friends major difference number  four his appearance  when it comes to the looks of a movie  character that's been adapted from a  book it's never going to be perfect  movies must deal with the process of  finding an actor who can play the part  while also keeping the novel's  description of the character in mind  i'm quite certain this ordeal is  somewhat of a nightmare in any case as  with the majority of characters who  appear first in books and later on in  movies there are some noticeable  differences between the look of novel  and film harry potter  of course both depictions of harry do  have his famous lightning bolt scar  naturally actor daniel radcliffe who as  mentioned earlier portrayed harry on the  big screen did not have this scar which  meant that the filmmakers were able to  choose exactly where to place it on  daniel's forehead however some fans of  the novels were upset upon seeing the  films since they had envisioned that the  scar was in the center of harry's  forehead however rest assured the scar  was where it was meant to be  as apparently it was jk rowling herself  who dictated where it should go on his  head  aside from the scar i suppose you could  say one other thing that's the same  between the two versions of harry is the  color of his hair  but in all honesty that's kind of where  the similarities stop  for the majority of the films daniel's  hair is pretty neat and tidy which is  not how harry's hair is described in the  books  in the novels his hair is said to be  wild and messy which i do concede they  kind of got right in the prisoner of  azkaban film  in any case at least they got the colour  right throughout the entire movie series  which is more than can be said about his  eye color  novel harry's eyes are well known to be  bright green  just like his mother's lilies  this detail of harry's appearance is  touched on many times throughout the  books  so it seems like it would have been a  given that whoever portrayed harry in  the films would also have a green eyes  even if that meant wearing coloured  contact lenses or something  and yet daniel radcliffe's harry potter  had clear blue eyes  well as it turns out daniel is allergic  to coloured contact lenses  so that option was out and i suppose for  such a small superficial part of harry's  appearance it didn't make sense to look  into any other options  the last difference between book and  movie harry's looks comes down to his  physique  quite honestly this doesn't bother me  too much since really how could you find  the perfect physical representation of a  character described in a book  but while we're on the topic of  differences i suppose i should admit  that i envisioned harry to be quite a  bit skinnier than he was in the films  and that's not to say that daniel  radcliffe isn't in shape rather daniel  just wasn't quite as thin and sharp in  appearance as i'd imagined harry would  be  as in the books he's described as having  knobbly knees and a thin face  neither of which are attributes of  daniel's  and with that we've come to the end of  another video  what did you think do you agree with the  differences i've suggested or have i  missed any major ones  let me know your thoughts in the  comments below and as always if you  enjoyed this video don't forget to like  it and subscribe to the channel until  next time remember  it does not do to dwell on dreams and  forget to live

